    Proposal to Change Release Schedule (#7122)
    
    As discussed during the German-speaking conference in Jena as well as
    the Dev meeting of 2025-09-23, I propose to shift
    the Release Schedule one month backwards starting with Opencast 20,
    meaning that all releases from that point onwards
    will happen one month earlier.
    
    That means that Opencast 20 would release in the middle of May instead
    of June, Opencast
    21 in the middle of November instead of December, and then so on. The
    exact release date will still be determined by the
    release managers.
    
    The reasons for this are as followed:
    - To give people from countries with an earlier semester start like
    Switzerland enough time to test before going
    productive.
    - To keep the major releases out of December, as that is a busy time for
    a lot of people.
